Most beneficiaries have Medicare Part B premiums deducted directly from their monthly Social Security benefits. When the Part B premium increases, it reduces the net gain from your annual cost-of-living adjustment (COLA).

The Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) fact sheet was published on November 17, 2026. The standard monthly Medicare Part B premium is $209.40 for 2027. That is a $6.50 increase over the $202.90 rate, alongside an annual deductible of $292.

You can review coverage rules on Medicare.gov. The Social Security Administration (SSA) delivers your exact net benefit amount to your [my Social Security](https://www.ssa.gov/myaccount/) Message Center in December.